vectors.txt: 600 test vectors (60 for each of ten model and format groups) written by tools/mfma-models/model_ref.py (`gen vectors.txt --n 60 --seed 1`).
The inputs are random and the answers are that script's: its author's second reading of the AMD models in
https://github.com/north-numerical-computing/MATLAB-tensor-core (models/MI100MC.m, MI210MC.m, MI300AMC.m and models/tools/Generic_BFMA_TC.m,
GEMM.m; commit 6fd0520850164bdd1c37f901954e27ec63eada56), paper: Khattak, Mikaitis and Graziani, "Accurate Models of AMD Matrix Cores",
arXiv 2609.14845. No file of that repository, and no data recorded on a card, is in this directory; MATLAB and Octave were not available, so
none of these answers was produced by the paper's own code. amd/src/mfma_models.hpp is written from the same files, not copied.

